# =============================================================================
# TwoPunctures geodesic probe, NEAR variant: tp_local27_025 (metric_interp=local27, no AEI thorns)
# TwoPunctures params = GW150914 (M+ =0.553846, M- =0.446153, b=5.0,
#   center_offset[0]=-0.53846, spins & momenta as set in this file).
# Cartesian 144^3, dx=0.25. No AMR (only diff vs GW150914 test).
# IC: ring r=8 with strong inward radial velocity (particle_* lines below).  Run 4p*20t.
# Purpose: near-field probe for the paper Sec. 5.6 rewrite — particles spiral
#   into the two punctures; the strong-field region yields NaN drops (a known
#   limitation of geodesic tracking this deep, not a code failure) and the
#   surviving trajectories wrap the black holes.
#   Part of the automatic validation suite (test/test.ccl, default set).
# =============================================================================
